WEBVTT

NOTE Re-timed to Piper narration (en_US-ljspeech-high, LJ Speech (Keith Ito), public domain). Native review still required.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:10.382
Paste a complete HTTP(S) link into Downloads. Choose the engine and quality,
then explicitly start. Demo only simulates progress and saves no media.

2
00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:17.458
Holding the waiting queue does not pause active jobs; cancellation and final
status are separate.

3
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:39.218
Protected media may require a supported decryption module and service
approval. Omnibloom never bypasses DRM or CAPTCHA. Use the service’s

4
00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:45.125
supported playback or download options; changing engines does not remove
protection.

5
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:09.568
If a request times out or the worker restarts, check the queue and history
before submitting again. A previous request may already have been accepted.

6
00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:15.125
Saved links keep the address; Use link fills the form without starting a
download.

7
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:39.852
Bloom Core runs in the background. If it is unavailable, apps should open
with their own defaults, but discovery and shared actions may be limited.

8
00:01:39.852 --> 00:01:45.032
Open the status page to see installed apps, versions and reported state.

9
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:11.332
For support include app build, firmware, PC system, controller model,
expected result, actual result and repeatable steps. Review logs before

10
00:02:11.332 --> 00:02:19.154
sharing; remove tokens, cookies, usernames, private URLs, device addresses
and personal paths.
